Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ===========================================================================
;  01_version_spoof.reg
;  Make the registry report VirtualBox 5.2.x so eNSP's version gate passes.
;
;  The machine actually has VirtualBox 7.2.x installed. eNSP refuses to talk to
;  anything that isn't 5.2.x, so the shim install rewrites only the Version /
;  VersionExt strings. InstallDir and PythonApiInstallDir are left untouched
;  (they already point at the real Oracle install).
;
;  eNSP opens this key with KEY_QUERY_VALUE | KEY_WOW64_64KEY (0x101): it reads
;  the 64-BIT view even though eNSP itself is 32-bit. The WOW6432Node view is
;  written too, for anything that reads it.
;
;  VersionExt must be byte-for-byte identical to Version, and must NOT carry a
;  build number. eNSP probes InstallDir's length once and reuses that same
;  cbData when it reads VersionExt; if VersionExt is longer than InstallDir,
;  RegQueryValueExW returns ERROR_MORE_DATA (234), eNSP reports
;  "Please check whether VirtualBox is installed." and the shim is never
;  loaded at all. Oracle's own installer writes both values without a build
;  number. Measured 2026-09-21 with InstallDir at 35 chars: 35 passes, 36 fails.
;
;  Adjust nothing here unless your VirtualBox install path differs.
; ===========================================================================

; --- 64-bit view -- the one eNSP reads ---
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Oracle\VirtualBox]
"Version"="5.2.44"
"VersionExt"="5.2.44"

; --- 32-bit view (WOW6432Node) ---
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\WOW6432Node\Oracle\VirtualBox]
"Version"="5.2.44"
"VersionExt"="5.2.44"
